r of mRNA expression of human oligodendrocyte-related genes involved in schizophrenia</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><year>2006</year><volume>103</volume><fpage>7482</fpage><lpage>7487</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16641098</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.0601213103</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aberg</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Saetre</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindholm</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ekholm</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Pettersson</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Adolfsson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Jazin</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human QKI, a new candidate gene for schizophrenia involved in myelination</article-title><source>Am J Med Genet B Neuropsychiatr Genet</source><year>2006</year><volume>141</volume><fpage>84</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16342280</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stevens</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neuropathology of schizophrenia</article-title><source>Arch Gen Psychiatry</source><year>1982</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>1131</fpage><lpage>1139</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7125843</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kenis</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bignotti</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Tura</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>De Jong</surname><given-names>R</